# examples/onus/: "Onus Oligarchiae", Oligarchy's theme, as a Standard MIDI
# File. stdout is the file, compared with `cmp`, byte for byte, with
# examples/onus/onus_oligarchiae.mid (7,897 bytes), which is WRITTEN BY
# prototypes/onus_oracle.py, not by this program:
#   python3 prototypes/onus_oracle.py examples/onus/onus_oligarchiae.mid
# The score is shared (partitura.exsc's tables are printed by
# `onus_oracle.py --exsc`); the encoding is not -- the oracle sorts
# absolute-time events and delta-codes them, the program walks each track
# as a stream with a carried delta and counts before it writes.
#
# The exit status is the program's own count: 0 only if all 7,897 bytes
# were written.
#
# Measured 2026-09-26: green in CI at 84db83d on the reference backend
# (compiles and assembles, exits 0, stdout byte-identical, syscall surface
# within {Mundus, ambitus}) and in the differential phase's four C builds.
# Its first CI run is what found the two defects the first draft had, both
# the compiler being right: `varius(s, c, (*c).mora)` is an aliased mutable
# argument (EXS-E0310), and `gradus`/`tactus` took 9 and 10 arguments where
# the Tier 1 emitter passes six -- hence the note riding in the pen.
# PROGRAM_FIXTURE_FLOOR is not raised here: the floor is set to measured
# suite counts, and this change measured one directory, not the suite.
#
# Before it compiled, a mechanical Python transliteration of the two files
# was the only check, and eight mutants of onus.exsc were run through it:
# seven change the bytes or the exit. The eighth -- the VLQ's third group
# firing at 16,385 instead of 16,384 -- is EQUIVALENT for this score, whose
# longest delta is 5,760 ticks; nothing here exercises a three-byte VLQ.
# Those mutants have not been re-run against the compiled program.
TEST: expect-exit=0 stdout=examples/onus/onus_oligarchiae.mid sources=examples/onus/partitura.exsc,examples/onus/onus.exsc
